#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133394 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57b95b5b-8834-5d1a-8380-fd8889e05cb4" :knowledge-point/title "Drawing the Graph of a Periodic Function"}] :question/id #uuid "1529ba15-ecf2-5c3f-871d-ab249ef9af34" :question/math-academy-id "e-1125" :question/problem "Part of the graph of a function $y=f(x)$ with period $2$ is shown below. What is the graph of $y=f(x)$ on the interval $-4\\leq x \\leq 4$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2148/Source/Images/ad24b9e538e0ef3e63637e496cfb9032.png)" :question/worked-solution "The graph above shows the function in the interval\n\n$$\n0 \\leq x \\leq 2\n$$\n\nSince this interval has length $2$, and the period of the function is also $2$, this interval represents a single period of the function.\n\nTherefore, the function will consist of many copies of the shape shown above, shifted horizontally by multiples of $2$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2148/Source/Images/bbdf4591cae648aba3d16286f3fd7d54.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57b95b5b-8834-5d1a-8380-fd8889e05cb4" :knowledge-point/title "Drawing the Graph of a Periodic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "808314c0-2c76-5761-889c-ce612d975d25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2148/Source/Images/q-41416-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132111} {:answer/id #uuid "89aa490e-11ae-517b-9d8c-1f4b7be57844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2148/Source/Images/q-41416-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132112} {:answer/id #uuid "9f40e48d-0489-5da6-8e5c-91bfe1d7eb83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2148/Source/Images/q-41416-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132113} {:answer/id #uuid "fea3f7dc-55a7-5215-be5d-1a03f8058ad9" 